Comparison with Exit-Controlled LoopsIn contrast, exit-controlled loops (like the do-while loop) evaluate the condition after the loop body executes, ensuring the loop body runs at least once regardless of the condition.Understanding entry-controlled loops is essential for writing effective and efficient code, as they provide a structured way to repeat operations while maintaining control over the conditions for repetition.Related ArticlesExit Controlled Loops in ProgrammingEntry vs Exit Controlled Loops in Programming
